0..78 Comment "//! Rules whose overlap parts at a call rather than a value are completed: the"
79..158 Comment "//! two rules of `swap` overlap at `swap(Zero, n)`, which one leaves at `n` and"
159..236 Comment "//! the other at `add(n, Zero)`, a call the written rules cannot rewrite with"
237..314 Comment "//! `n` unknown. Completion derives the rule joining the pair, `add(n, Zero)`"
315..389 Comment "//! rewriting to `n`, which follows from the written rules (both sides are"
390..443 Comment "//! reducts of one peak), and decides the pairs again"
444..524 Comment "//! [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras], § 7. The kernel reads"
525..588 Comment "//! the derived rule beside the written ones as one of `add`\'s."
589..592 Comment "//!"
593..608 Comment "//! - see: #338"
609..674 Comment "//! - cites: [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]"
675..678 Comment "//!"
679..850 Comment "//! [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]: https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-08-012975-4.50028-X \"Knuth and Bendix, Simple Word Problems in Universal Algebras\""
